const e=[{id:1,title:"New publication on BEXIS2 as a FAIR-aligned research data management system",author:"Roman Gerlach",date:"2021/11/02",content:'<p>Can BEXIS2 support you in making your research data compatible with Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable (FAIR) data principles?</p><p>The new publication BEXIS2: A FAIR-aligned data management system for biodiversity, ecology, and environmental data by Chamanara et al. demonstrates how are the FAIR data principles integrated into the BEXIS2 application.</p><p>The paper also presents community deployment examples of the BEXIS2 instances to explain its capacity to meet the data management needs of differently sized projects and serve as an organizational research data management system.</p><p>The authors of the paper are grateful to the developers who contributed to the development of the BEXIS2 over the years; the current and previous data managers and curators for providing the feedback to improve the usability of the BEXIS2 system; Th\xFCringer Universit\xE4ts und Landesbibliothek Jena for providing the Open Access Publication Fund.</p><p><b>Citation:</b></p><p>Chamanara J, Gaikwad J, Gerlach R, Algergawy A, Ostrowski A, K\xF6nig-Ries B (2021) BEXIS2: A FAIR-aligned data management system for biodiversity, ecology and environmental data. Biodiversity Data Journal 9: e72901. <a target="blank" href="https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.9.e72901">https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.9.e72901</p>'},{id:2,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.14.5",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2021/10/22",content:'<p>Before you rush off into the weekend, wait a minute. Here\u2019s some great news. We have released a small but nice new patch.</p><p>Yes, BEXIS2 2.14.5 is now available.</p><p><b>Attention:</b> Changes were made in the web.config in line: 72 (see <a href="https://github.com/BEXIS2/Core/issues/803">#803</a>)</p><p>Look forward to Monday and have fun with BEXIS2 stay healthy.</p><p>BEXIS2.14.5 is now available >>> <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.14.5">here</a> <<<'},{id:3,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.14.4",author:"Sven Thiel",date:"2021/05/17",content:'<p>From the home office, we send greetings and wish you good health. To make the challenging time a little more bearable, we send, besides the greetings also a patch for BEXIS2 that you should not miss.</p><p>Attention! Changes have been made in SMTP credentials and web.config. If an update is made, please use the new files and adapt them.</p><p>BEXIS2.14.4 is now available on our GitHub page: <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.14.4">here</a>.'},{id:3,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.14.6",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2022/06/30",content:'<p>BEXIS2.14.6 is now available on our github page: <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.14.6">here</a>.'},{id:4,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.15",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2022/08/25",content:'<p> Even though the sun is shining outside, we have continued to work. :D So we can release the new version earlier than expected.</p><p>BEXIS2.15 is now available on our github page: <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.15">here</a>.'},{id:5,title:"BEXIS2: a system for FAIR and reproducible research data management workshop at the FORSCHUNGSDATEN@RMU 2022",author:"Jitendra Gaikwad",date:"2022/10/12",content:'<p>During the workshop, we demonstrated the working of the BEXIS2 and provided hands-on experience of using BEXIS2 as to potential data managers or system administrators. The workshop was attended by 19 participants.</p><p>The program is available  <a href="https://www.forschungsdaten.uni-mainz.de/files/2022/09/Programm-FORSCHUNGSDATENatRMU-2022.pdf">here</a>'},{id:6,title:"NFDI ToolTalk: BEXIS2 Research Data Management System",author:"Jitendra Gaikwad",date:"2022/10/17",content:'<p>As part of the NFDI INFRA Talk series, Roman Gerlach gave a talk on BEXIS2 Research Data Management System.</p><p>The talk is now available on the NFDI YouTube Channel >>> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7jMGRS1_m2c">here</a><<<</p>'},{id:7,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.16",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2022/11/01",content:`<p>Hold on, it's not Christmas yet, but there's a new release anyway.</p><p>BEXIS2.16 is now available on our GitHub page: <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.16">here</a>.</p>`},{id:8,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.17",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2023/02/23",content:`<p>Hi y'all, we are glad to inform you that we have released the new version 2.17 of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.17">here</a> for more details.</p>`},{id:9,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.18",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2023/04/27",content:`<p>Hi y'all, we are glad to inform you that we have released the new version 2.18 of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.18">here</a> for more details.</p>`},{id:11,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.18.1",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2023/06/28",content:'<p>We are glad to inform you that we have released the new version 2.18.1 of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.18.1">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:9,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 2.18.2",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2023/09/26",content:'<p>We are glad to inform you that we have released the new version 2.18.2 of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#2.18.2">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:9,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.0.0-beta",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2023/12/22",content:'<p>We are glad to inform you that we have released a new major version (3.0.0-beta) of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.0.0-beta">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:10,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.1.0",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2024/03/12",content:'<p>This release focused on fixing found bugs or already identified necessary changes in version 3.0.0-beta. Thanks to all testing version 3.0.0-beta!.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.1.0">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:11,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.2.0",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2024/04/17",content:'<p>This release focused on updating UI libraries, fixing bugs, adding new constraint features, and adding the first version of the new primary data for testing.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.2.0">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:12,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.2.1",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2024/04/25",content:'<p>In this release two bugs were fixed for the mapping and delete dataset landing page.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.2.1">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:13,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.3.0",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2024/07/02",content:'<p>It took us a bit longer, but BEXIS2 version 3.3.0 also has exciting new features! The first is the Darwin Core Archive Export, which is now possible entirely via the UI of BEXIS2 (metadata & data). The second bigger feature is the integration of a DOI workflow, which allows issuing DOIs at DataCite (your institutional account is required). Further, BEXIS2 instance can now define their own landing page and use an external metadata form to enter metadata. As part of our new release procedure we updated libraries, but also improved authentication options needed for our future development and fixed several bugs. </p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.3.0">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:14,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.3.1",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2024/08/26",content:'<p>We are glad to inform you that we have released the new version 3.3.1 of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look at <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.3.3.1">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:15,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.3.2",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2024/09/04",content:'<p>We are glad to inform you that we have released the new version 3.3.2 of BEXIS2.</p><p>Please take a look <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.3.2">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:16,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 3.4.0",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2024/09/27",content:'<p>We are happy to inform you that we added several new cool features to BEXIS2, improved several pages, fixed bugs, and also took care of maintenance and security issues.</p><p>Please take a look <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#3.4.0">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:17,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 4.0.0",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2025/04/04",content:'<p>We are happy to inform you that this version mainly contains fixed bugs and usability improvements of the new functions and features, focusing on the area of dataset creation and upload introduced since version 3.0.0. and a refactored documentation.</p><p>Please take a look <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#4.0.0">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:18,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 4.0.1",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2025/04/22",content:'<p>We are happy to inform you that we released a small bugfix version for which also add new seed data for DOI issuing.</p><p>Please take a look <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#4.0.1">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:19,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 4.0.2",author:"Franziska Zander",date:"2025/05/12",content:'<p>We are happy to inform you that we fixed some bugs.</p><p>Please take a look <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#4.0.2">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:20,title:"BEXIS2 Release - 4.1.0",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2025/08/21",content:'<p>This release comes with a big reduction in data type complexity by removing unused and redundant data types. Only the most commonly used data types are now available, which simplifies the data structure creation process. Additionally, this release includes several bug fixes and enhancements to improve the overall user experience. Further we introduced a new setting to control sending error emails based from the system.</p><p>Please take a look <a href="https://bexis2.github.io/software/releases#4.1.0">here</a> for more details.</p>'},{id:21,title:"TKFDM Coffee Lecture",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2023/07/19",content:'<p>Roman Gerlach gave a presentation on BEXIS2 at the Forschungsdatenmanagement Th\xFCringen (TKFD) coffee lecture. The video is available here.</p><p>The presentation is available<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TtLm_1mf3LU&t=1s">here</a>.</p>'},{id:22,title:"LAND Community Workshop 2025",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2025/01/21",content:"<p>David Sch\xF6ne had the honor of giving a BEXIS2 hands-on workshop at the \u201CLAND Community Workshop 2025\u201D in Leipzig.</p>"},{id:23,title:"Uni Trier",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2025/01/31",content:"<p>In Leipzig, we had the wonderful opportunity to collaborate with the University of Trier. During the workshop, we delved deep into the creation of data structures and the uploading of data.</p>"},{id:24,title:"HeFDI Data Talk",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2025/03/04",content:`<p>Our team was delighted to recently hold a presentation on BEXIS2, the open-source data management system, as part of <b>the HeFDI Data Talks series</b>. The event, "BEXIS2 - Funktionale \xDCbersicht und Demo," gave us the opportunity to showcase the system's key features and demonstrate its user-friendly interface. We explored how BEXIS2 helps researchers efficiently manage, document, and share their data, particularly for projects in biodiversity and environmental sciences. The presentation was a great success, and we thank the HeFDI team and everyone who attended for their active participation and insightful questions.</p><p>The presentaion is available <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tyqpHj5AGKY&t=311s">here</a>.</p>`},{id:25,title:"NFDIBiodiversity Tools & Services",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2025/05/08",content:`<p>During the <b>NFDI4Biodiversity Tools & Services</b> webinar, David Sch\xF6ne presented the free, open-source data management system, <b>BEXIS2</b>. His presentation, titled 'BEXIS2 - A free, open-source software that supports researchers in data management,' showed attendees how the software effectively assists researchers with their data management tasks.</b>. The event, "BEXIS2 - Funktionale \xDCbersicht und Demo," gave us the opportunity to showcase the system's key features and demonstrate its user-friendly interface. We explored how BEXIS2 helps researchers efficiently manage, document, and share their data, particularly for projects in biodiversity and environmental sciences. The presentation was a great success, and we thank the HeFDI team and everyone who attended for their active participation and insightful questions.</p><p>The presentation is available <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tyqpHj5AGKY&t=311s">here</a>.</p>`},{id:26,title:"Bridging Data and People: BEXIS2 in Focus at FDM-Tage 2025",author:"David Sch\xF6ne",date:"2025/07/19",content:'<p>At the recent FDM-Tage 2025, Cornelia F\xFCrstenau (Data Manager, Biodiversity Exploratories) and David Sch\xF6ne (BEXIS2 Developer) gave a joint presentation titled <b>"Bridging Data and People: BEXIS2 Through Two Lenses."</b></p><p>They offered a unique perspective on the BEXIS2 research data management system, showing its functions from two different angles: the end-user and the data manager. This combined approach highlighted how the software effectively addresses the needs of various user groups.</p><p>The presentation is available <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iYxLBBrwduk&t=350s">here</a>.'}];export{e as n};
